{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0b8cfa5027d68c9418e5fb57cad0af4582214eff7d4091b31e4b770ce05e1573"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"No vector database is used yet (planned for storing/retrieving codebase and CVE info), and only the CVE description is used today, with exploit POCs planned as future sources."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ae5a092ca4163cdc227241bde65439e200428953d2640dcbabf7df24b5eac25"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites include Python 3.12.3, a GitHub API token, and a locally running Ollama instance with the Mistral 7B model; a CUDA GPU is listed as needed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_59062f6d2de2b2fca6577dbfbbf37b8461d9c3233728b751a70eeb6b4fe5e5f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions are welcome via pull requests, per the README's contributing section."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d19c2efb806ef58a31c6ce0e2a157db43520f9019122e58fa45f275c3e45d98"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A multi-agent system includes GithubAdvisoryTool (fetches/parses CVE info), SecurityAnalystAgent (Mistral-based component identification), ComponentSearcherTool (codebase scan), and CodeReviewerAgent (impact analysis)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a055c4cc76268e03cf0c7c3d07d1c469dca32a318ac1ae23d96fa695d43855f1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI is invoked as python3 cve_analyzer.py with a GHSA advisory ID and a path to the codebase as arguments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a78d14add337d717229932318a51532d463af3ec27f7588edffe0ea87e8dea83"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The AI solution is designed to run fully on-premises so that no data leaves the user's premises."},{"claim_ids":["clm_aa2d8e40c4a0cf9bd8e776afaa2ba1c154375bcde55dac1d0841dfa3f55f5fe3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool targets teams triaging SBOM/Dependabot vulnerability alerts; the demo analyzes GHSA advisories against a sample CTF challenge repository."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e74aac804ec9ca80621c04e5699e40366a7f70d1a8191b154ffd934e646cb873"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool performs intelligent impact analysis on reported vulnerabilities to reduce the false positives that traditional SCA tools generate from relying only on SBOM data."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eb2a35740d7883763ba14090fd4cbaebcafb0f9cd638377f0b611fe82ad2eb89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup involves cloning the repo, creating a .env file with GITHUB_TOKEN, ensuring Ollama runs the Mistral model, and installing packages via pip install -r requirements.txt."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f5661ecd2ecca32d3ccd01c412a92a324848446b771a339d9eccfaa3fbfe792a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is currently tested only on Python codebases, per the README's limitations section."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fea4cb913904934f27db3af6118aa1d0a141455b5e3ac39179dbccb1a5b1ac58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system uses agentic AI powered by the open-source Mistral model and includes a human-in-the-loop model for accuracy and control."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0b8cfa5027d68c9418e5fb57cad0af4582214eff7d4091b31e4b770ce05e1573","clm_3ae5a092ca4163cdc227241bde65439e200428953d2640dcbabf7df24b5eac25","clm_59062f6d2de2b2fca6577dbfbbf37b8461d9c3233728b751a70eeb6b4fe5e5f0","clm_9d19c2efb806ef58a31c6ce0e2a157db43520f9019122e58fa45f275c3e45d98","clm_a055c4cc76268e03cf0c7c3d07d1c469dca32a318ac1ae23d96fa695d43855f1","clm_a78d14add337d717229932318a51532d463af3ec27f7588edffe0ea87e8dea83","clm_aa2d8e40c4a0cf9bd8e776afaa2ba1c154375bcde55dac1d0841dfa3f55f5fe3","clm_e74aac804ec9ca80621c04e5699e40366a7f70d1a8191b154ffd934e646cb873","clm_eb2a35740d7883763ba14090fd4cbaebcafb0f9cd638377f0b611fe82ad2eb89","clm_f5661ecd2ecca32d3ccd01c412a92a324848446b771a339d9eccfaa3fbfe792a","clm_fea4cb913904934f27db3af6118aa1d0a141455b5e3ac39179dbccb1a5b1ac58"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:32:50Z","created_by_operation":"op_1814e823755e4b37adff6f70172cc6c5","id":"pg_1bc7c86f2e2b5b8c8c8cb1a1c8b3236f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/alexdevassy-ai-powered-vulnerability-impact